---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  fullTitle="About ChineseMenu — A Traveler's Chinese Menu Decoder"
  description="Who builds ChineseMenu, how we research dish names, pinyin and prices, and why every recommendation on the site is independent with no paid placements."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-5xl">
      About ChineseMenu
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      ChineseMenu is a free traveler's tool that helps you read, translate and
      order real Chinese dishes — in English, Chinese characters and pinyin, with
      typical prices and a printable point-to-order card.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Our mission</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We built this after watching too many first-time visitors stare at a
          wall of Chinese characters and order by blind pointing. The goal is
          simple: give you the picture, the name, the price and the phrase — so
          the moment you sit down, you already know what you want.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Who writes and verifies this</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          ChineseMenu is researched and written by an editorial team of long-time
          China residents — travel writers, native Mandarin editors and food
          researchers — who verify dish names, pinyin and prices against real
          menus in Beijing, Chengdu, Shanghai and beyond.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Prices are typical mainland-China ranges, refreshed every quarter. City
          guides draw on well-known food streets and the dishes locals actually
          order. Chengdu is a
          <a
            href="https://en.unesco.org/creative-cities/chengdu"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700">UNESCO City of Gastronomy</a
          >, one of the official sources we cross-check.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">How we make money</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We do not sell placements. No restaurant pays to appear anywhere on
          this site, and no dish is sponsored. Every recommendation is made
          independently on merit. The site is supported by affiliate links to
          travel tools where clearly marked; these never influence what we list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Get in touch</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Questions, corrections or dish suggestions are welcome — reader
          questions often become new guides. Email the editorial team at
          <a
            href="mailto:contact@chinese-menus.com"
            class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700">contact@chinese-menus.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
